---
// Dev-only preview of the conversation components (injected at /_components under
// `astro dev`; never built). Lines come from docs/copy.md.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import UserLine from '../components/UserLine.astro';
import ProductLine from '../components/ProductLine.astro';
import Receipt from '../components/Receipt.astro';
import PhoneFrame from '../components/PhoneFrame.astro';
---

<Base title="Components">
  <div class="container-page space-y-16 py-16">
    <section class="space-y-6">
      <h2>Lines, size lg (hero)</h2>
      <UserLine size="lg">I'm building food delivery for college hostels. Swiggy made it, so will I.</UserLine>
      <ProductLine size="lg">Love the confidence. Quick question first: who's paying? The students, or their parents' UPI?</ProductLine>
      <ProductLine size="lg">
        Also, Swiggy is one survivor. We found three hostel-delivery startups that didn't make it. Want to meet them?
        <Receipt>3 similar startups, why they shut down, sources linked</Receipt>
      </ProductLine>
      <ProductLine size="lg">Your call. Always.</ProductLine>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-6">
      <h2>Lines, size md (FAQ)</h2>
      <UserLine speaker={false}>Isn't this just ChatGPT with an attitude?</UserLine>
      <ProductLine speaker={false}>
        Most chatbots are trained to be agreeable. We're built to find the other side, and we bring receipts: a curated
        database of failed startups and the actual texts of philosophers, with every quote checked.
      </ProductLine>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-6">
      <h2>Phone frame, size sm</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-10">
        <PhoneFrame label="Mockup: step 6 in idea mode" subtitle="Challenge my idea" caption="Illustrative mockup.">
          <UserLine size="sm">Food delivery for college hostels. Swiggy did it, so there's clearly demand.</UserLine>
          <ProductLine size="sm">
            The real question: does demand survive 3 months of holidays a year? Bias spotted: survivorship. You're
            looking at Swiggy, not the graveyard.
          </ProductLine>
          <UserLine size="sm">But we'll do breakfast subscriptions!</UserLine>
          <ProductLine size="sm">
            Interesting. Subscriptions fix vacation dips only if parents prepay a semester. Would they?
          </ProductLine>
        </PhoneFrame>
        <PhoneFrame label="Mockup: step 5 in decision mode" subtitle="Challenge my decision" caption="Paraphrases, not quotes.">
          <UserLine size="sm">I'm skipping placements to build my startup full time.</UserLine>
          <ProductLine size="sm" bodyAs="div">
            <p>Many traditions prize courage and writing your own story.</p>
            <p>
              <Receipt>Aristotle, Nicomachean Ethics, Book VI</Receipt> Practical wisdom means weighing your
              circumstances, not just your desire.
            </p>
            <p>
              <Receipt>Seneca, Letters to Lucilius</Receipt> Rehearse the worst case before you act, so it can't ambush
              you.
            </p>
          </ProductLine>
        </PhoneFrame>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
